---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Before We Record"
  description="What to expect, and what to have ready, when you record an episode of Arrested DevOps."
  noindex
>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="badge">BEFORE WE RECORD</div>
    <h1>Here's what to expect when we record.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Thanks for coming on Arrested DevOps. This is the whole checklist, and none of it is a test.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        We book an hour. The episode itself usually runs 30 to 40 minutes, and the rest is for hellos
        and a sound check.
      </p>
      <p>
        We record both audio and video. If you'd rather not be on camera, tell us before the day and we'll
        make it an audio-only episode.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Joining</h2>
      <p>
        Your calendar invite has the studio link in the location field, and the agenda doc is attached to
        the same invite. Click the link a few minutes early. You don't need an account or an app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chrome, Edge, Arc, Firefox, and Safari 26 or later all work. If you're on a Mac with an older
        Safari, use Chrome. Your browser will ask to use your microphone and camera, so say yes. You can
        join with the camera off if you want.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>What to have ready</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Headphones, wired if you have them. Wired ones are the most reliable, and they keep the sound
          from echoing. Bluetooth works, but it can drop audio quality or disconnect mid-episode.
        </li>
        <li>A quiet, well-lit spot, with your face in front of the camera.</li>
        <li>
          A solid connection. A wired one is best. On Wi-Fi, sit near the router and close extra apps and
          tabs. Aim for at least 10 Mbps up and down.
        </li>
        <li>An external microphone or camera, if you have one. Your laptop's will do if you don't.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>The agenda</h2>
      <p>
        The doc attached to your invite is a list of things we might ask about. It isn't a script, and you
        don't need to prepare.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>When we stop</h2>
      <p>
        Your recording uploads as we go. After we finish, stay in the room until the upload confirmation
        appears on your screen, then close the tab. If it stalls, let us know.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Odds and ends</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Need to move it? Use the reschedule link in your confirmation email.
        </li>
        <li>
          Haven't sent your bio and headshot yet? It takes a few minutes:
          <a href="/guestform/">the guest info form</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Anything else:
          <a href="mailto:shows@arresteddevops.com">shows@arresteddevops.com</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1,
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .intro {
    padding: 64px var(--page-padding) 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    background: var(--color-red-deep);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .content {
    padding: 24px var(--page-padding) 64px;
    max-width: 800px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .card {
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-navy);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card-lg);
    padding: 28px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    background: var(--color-cream-card);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .card p,
  .card li {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-red-deep);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 38px;
    }

    .card {
      padding: 22px 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
